{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.borromean_hopf_energy_crossover","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.borromean_hopf_energy_crossover","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic"],"declarations":10,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.borromean_hopf_energy_crossover","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.borromean_hopf_energy_crossover","kind":"def","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/borromean_hopf_energy_crossover.lean#L48-L138","doc":"**Manuscript statement** (full body):\n\n**Proposition.**\nLet $q > 1$ be the substrate parameter and $\\hbar_q = (q-1)/q$.\nConsider $6$ quarks (two baryon-number units) with flavor content\n$(\\mathfrak{u}, \\mathfrak{d}, \\mathfrak{s})^{\\otimes 2}$.  These\n$6$ quarks can be assembled in two topologically distinct\nconfigurations:\n\n- **Borromean phase** ($\\mathcal{P}_B$): two Borromean baryons\n  $\\mathcal{B}_3 \\cdot \\mathcal{B}_3$, each with Borromean\n  volume $V_B = 7.32772$ and inter-baryon Hopf binding.\n\n- **Diquark phase** ($\\mathcal{P}_D$): three Hopf diquark\n  pairs ([Hopf diquark](#def:hopf-diquark))\n  $D_{[\\mathfrak{u}\\mathfrak{d}]} \\cdot D_{[\\mathfrak{d}\\mathfrak{s}]} \\cdot D_{[\\mathfrak{s}\\mathfrak{u}]}$, each bound by $\\mathcal{L}_H$.\n\nThen:\n\n1. **Mass comparison.**  The Borromean phase has mass\n\n$$\n  M_B\n  = \n  2 \\cdot \\frac{V_B}{\\hbar_q^2}\n  = \n  \\frac{2 \\times 7.32772}{((q-1)/q)^2}\n  = \n  \\frac{14.6554 q^2}{(q-1)^2}.\n$$\n\n   The diquark phase has mass from crossing energy only\n   (Hopf link volume is zero):\n\n$$\n  M_D\n  = \n  3 \\cdot \\tfrac{1}{3}(q + q^{-1})\n  = \n  q + q^{-1}\n   \\approx  2.011  \\text{Skein units}.\n$$\n\n   Since $\\mathrm{Vol}(\\mathcal{L}_H) = 0$, the diquark\n   mass is **purely from crossing energy**, not from\n   hyperbolic volume.  At any $q > 1$: $M_D \\ll M_B$.\n\n2. **Binding energy comparison.**  The binding energy\n   per baryon number is:\n\n   - Borromean: $\\mathfrak{E}_B = -V_B / \\hbar_q^2$ (from\n     Borromean volume)\n   - Diquark: $\\mathfrak{E}_D = -\\tfrac{3}{2}(q + q^{-1})$\n     (from three Hopf links shared between two baryon-number\n     units, strong channel only since the CFL condensate is\n     color-neutral)\n\n   The crossover occurs when $|\\mathfrak{E}_D| > |\\mathfrak{E}_B|$,\n   i.e., when the Hopf-link binding per baryon number exceeds\n   the Borromean binding:\n\n$$\n  \\frac{3}{2}(q + q^{-1})\n   > \n  \\frac{V_B}{\\hbar_q^2}\n  = \n  \\frac{7.32772 q^2}{(q-1)^2}.\n$$\n\n3. **At $q = q_0$.**\n\n$$\n  \\frac{3}{2}(q + q^{-1})\n  = \n  \\frac{3}{2}(q_0 + q_0^{-1})\n  = \n  \\frac{3}{2} \\times 2.0108\n  =  3.\n\n[…truncated; see manuscript for remainder…]\n\n    The proposition is **named** below as a `def … : Prop` (pattern C):\n    `V_B` and the energy-comparison predicate are opaque inputs, so the\n    three-part claim is recorded as the conditional conjecture over the\n    context rather than discharged by a fake projection. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:borromean-hopf-energy-crossover","label":"prop:borromean-hopf-energy-crossover","md":"quantum-observable-universe/observations/borromean-hopf-energy-crossover.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BorromeanHopfEnergyCrossoverContext.E_D","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BorromeanHopfEnergyCrossoverContext.E_D","kind":"def","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/borromean_hopf_energy_crossover.lean#L46-L46","doc":"Binding energy per baryon-number in the diquark phase. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BorromeanHopfEnergyCrossoverContext.E_B","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BorromeanHopfEnergyCrossoverContext.E_B","kind":"def","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/borromean_hopf_energy_crossover.lean#L44-L44","doc":"Binding energy per baryon-number in the Borromean phase. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BorromeanHopfEnergyCrossoverContext.M_D","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BorromeanHopfEnergyCrossoverContext.M_D","kind":"def","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/borromean_hopf_energy_crossover.lean#L42-L42","doc":"Mass of the Hopf-diquark phase. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BorromeanHopfEnergyCrossoverContext.M_B","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BorromeanHopfEnergyCrossoverContext.M_B","kind":"def","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/borromean_hopf_energy_crossover.lean#L40-L40","doc":"Mass of the Borromean phase (two `B_3` baryons + inter-baryon Hopf\nbinding). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BorromeanHopfEnergyCrossoverContext.V_B","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BorromeanHopfEnergyCrossoverContext.V_B","kind":"def","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/borromean_hopf_energy_crossover.lean#L37-L37","doc":"Borromean hyperbolic volume `V_B ≈ 7.32772`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BorromeanHopfEnergyCrossoverContext.q_gt_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BorromeanHopfEnergyCrossoverContext.q_gt_one","kind":"theorem","line":35,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/borromean_hopf_energy_crossover.lean#L35-L35","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BorromeanHopfEnergyCrossoverContext.q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BorromeanHopfEnergyCrossoverContext.q","kind":"def","line":34,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/borromean_hopf_energy_crossover.lean#L34-L34","doc":"Substrate parameter `q : ℝ` (`q > 1`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BorromeanHopfEnergyCrossoverContext.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BorromeanHopfEnergyCrossoverContext.mk","kind":"ctor","line":32,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/borromean_hopf_energy_crossover.lean#L32-L32","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BorromeanHopfEnergyCrossoverContext","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BorromeanHopfEnergyCrossoverContext","kind":"class","line":29,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/borromean_hopf_energy_crossover.lean#L29-L46","doc":"Abstract context (inputs) for the `borromean_hopf_energy_crossover`\nclaim — the substrate parameter, the Borromean volume, and the two\nphase masses and binding energies.  No field asserts a conclusion. ","signatureChunk":0}]}